        <p>THE WARRINGTON EXAMINER published every Saturday morning. The principal and the oldest weekly paper for War- rington, Stockton Heath, Penketh, Winwick, Padgate Lymm, &amp;c., being one of the largest and best weekly papers in Lancashire and Cheshire. The district covered by this paper comprises a large trading and agricultural tract in South Lancashire and Mid- Cheshire. MHE RUNCORN EXAMINER, published every Saturday morning. It is the best weekly paper in Town and district, and offers the best and cheapest facilities to advertisers. THE WIDNES EXAMINER, published every Saturday morning. Widnes contains the largest number of chemical works of any town in the Kingdom, and is a rapidly growing centre of industry. THE EARLESTOWN AND NEWTON EXAMINER, published every Saturday morning. The largest local paper containing the news of Earlestown, Newton-le-Willows, Golborne, Hay-dock, Lowton, &amp;c The district thus comprised is a most important part of the Lancashire coalfields. • THE ST. HELENS EXAMINER, published every Saturday morning, circulating in St. Helens, Prescot," Parr, Sutton, Peasley Cross, &amp;c.—the centre of the glass, chemical and watch trades of the Kingdom.</p>
