        <p>DISTRICT CLASSES.—Brood Mare having produced a living foal by, or stinted to, a registered hackney sire in 1909.—First prize, £5; second, £3; third, £2. Sir Gilbert Greenall. Bart., gives a premium of £3 for the test 'exhibit belonging to a tenant farmer: 1, Sir Lees Knowles,Bart.C.V.O. ; 2,John Makeague,Golborne Park, Newton-le-Willows; 3, Sir Lees Knowles, Rat. ; r, Whittaker and Oliver, Agdeo,Lymm ; li c and premium, Joshua Ball, Southworth Hall, Warrington. Foal by a registered hackney sire.—First prize, £4; second, £3; third, £2: 1, Whittaker and Oliver, Agden, Lymm ;2, John Makeague, Golborne Park, Newton-le-Willows; 3, Sir Lee Knowles,Bart.,C.V.O.,Westwood,Pendiebury; r, James B. Aitken, Hall Nook. Penketh. Yearling Colt, Gelding or Filly, by a registered hickney sire.—First prize, £4; second; £3; third, £2: 1, Joshua Ball, Southworth Hall ; 2, Bentley and Sons, 16, Canute- place, Knutsford ; 3, William Brown, Seven Stars, Warrington. Two-year-old Gelding or Filly by a registered hackney sire.—First prize, £4 ; second, £3; third, £2: 1, William Johnson, Acresfield Stud, Wootton; 2, Alfred Smith, Stud Farm,Crank, Stßelens; 3, Richard Billington. Brookside Farm, Stretton. Three- year-old Gelding or Filly, by a registered hackney sire. —First prize, £4; second, £3 ; third, £2: I, John .Makeague, Golborne Park; 2, Whittaker and Oliver, Agden, Lymm ; 3, Sir Lees Knowles, Part.: r, James McWaters„ Hale Bank, near Widnes. Pony Brood Mare not exeeeding 14 hands, having produced a living foal by, or stintdd to, a registered hacknu, or registeerd hackney pony stallion in I9o9.—First prize, £5 ; second, ; third, £2. Sir Gilbeti; Greenall, Bart., gives a premium of £3 for the best exhibit belonging to a tenant farmer : 1, Miss M. E. Knott, St. Martins, Heaton; 2, Alfred Smith, Stud Farm, Crank, Stßelens; 3, Mrs. L. Proctor, Mere Hall, Cheshire; premium, Sam W. Gould, Foxley Hall, Lymm ; r, John Makeague, Golborne, Park, Newton-le-Willovrs. Foal by registered hackney, or registered hackney pony stallion, out of a mare entered in class 25.—First prize, £4; s2cond, £3; third, £2: 1, Miss M. E. Knott, St. Martin's, Hooton ; 2, Alfred Smith, Stud Farm, Crank, St. Helens; 3, Frank Cash, Hale, Cheshire; r, Mrs. L. Proctor, Mere Hall, Mere,Cheshire.</p>
