        <p>DISTRICT CLASSES.—Light Horses (single or pair) vehicle aud harness.—First prize, £5; second, £3; third, £2; fourth, ,E 1 : 1, William Hall, 95, Peter-street, St. Helens; 2, Edward Holmes and Sons, Stretton ; 3, John Garth, Prescot Corn Mills, Prescot ; equal, 4, Mrs. Mary Ellen French, 112, Liverpool-road, St. Helens; 4, Thomas Warburton, hall Lane Farm, Daresbury.</p>
        <p>Vanners or Light Lutry Horses (single or pair) vehicle and harness.—keirst prize, £5; second, £3; third, £2; fourth, £1: 1, Willihm Blackshaw, Greenside Farm, Hatton; 2, Esors. of Joseph CAldwell, Froghall Bakery, Warrington ;3, T. H. Fairhurst, Hatton, Warrington; 4, John H. Crosby, Collins Green Farm, Burtonwood. Single Heavy Horse, vehicle and harness, belonging to Tradesmsn.—First prize, £5; second, El; third, £2; fourth, El : 1, The Warrington Corporation; 2, George Howard, 2, Bennett-street, ‘S'arringron. Single Heavy Horse, vehicle and harness, belonging to a Tenant Farmer. No horse in this class has ever been awarded a first prize at any show (sales excepted) previous to 10th August, 1909.—First prize, £5; second, £3; third, £2; fourth, £1: 1, Dan Massey, Crumley Heath, Little Leigh, Northwich ; 2, Edward Davies, Walk Farm, Partington ; 3, Thomas W3rburton, Hall Lane Farm, Daresbury ; 4 (equal), R. L. Warburton, Hatton, War- rington; Exors. John Blackshaw, Blue Coat farm, Hatton; George Blackshaw, Church Farm, Stretton.</p>
        <p>* CATTLE. DISTRICT CLASSES.—Dairy COW in Calf (to calve within 2 months after date of Show). First prize, £4; second, £3; third, I 2 : 1, Dan Massey, Crumley Heath, Little Leigh, Northwich; 2 and 3, Sam S. Raingill, The Grange, Ringway, Altrincharn ; h.c.Mrs. Fiances Cowap. Bowling Green, Little Leigh; r, Herbert Beech, Smoker Hill Farm, Plumbley, near Knutsford. Dairy Cow in Milk.—First prize, £4; second, £3; third, £2. 1 and 2, Sam S. Raingill, The Grange, Ringway, Altrincham ; 3, Frank Smith, Woolton, Liverpool; h c, Samuel Davies, Platt Farm Heatley • r, Herbert Beech, Smoker Hill Farm, PI umbley, near knutsford. Heifer born in 1907.— First pi ize, £1; second, £3 ; third, £2: 1, Sim W. Gould, Foley HaM, Lymm ; 2, William Norcott, Four Topped Oak, Penketh-for-Bold, Warrington. Heifer born in 1908.—First prize, £4 ; second, £3; third, £2 : 1, William Norcott, Four Topped Oak, Penketh-for- Bold, Warrington; 2, William Conper, Cl iyton's Farm, Bartonwood, near Newton-le-Nillows. Bull, under 2 years.—First prize, £5 ; second, £3 ; £2: 1, Sam S. Raingill, The Grange, Ringway, Altrincham ; 2, Richard Clarke, Warburton Park, near Warrington • 3, Arthur Platt, Wincham, near Northwich; r, C. L. Agnew, The Pole, Northwich, Cheshire. Bull, over 2 years.—First prize, £5; second, £3; third, £3: 1, Ralph Tickle, Hill Side Farm, Appleton, NVarrington ; 2, C. L. Agnew, The Pole, Northwich, Cheshire; 3, J. K. Priestner, Porch House Farm, Acton Grange.</p>
