        <p>District Champion Cup (value £10) given by Sir Gilbert Greenall, Bart,' for the best mare or filly : James Gould ; r, Lewis Dodd. Silver Cup (value £5) given by Sir Gilbert Greenall, Bart., for the best shire foal : James Gould. Silver Cop (value £5) given by Sir Gilbert Greenall, Bart., for the best shire exhibit, the property of one of his tenants: A. Broome; r R. L. Warburton, Hatton. Special Prize (value 25; given by Mr. F. Stapleton Bretherton, for the best shire filly: Lewis Dodd. Silver Cup (value 5 guineas) given by Mr. T. Henry Lyon for the best. dairy cow : S. S. Raingill. Silver Cap (value £5), given by Mr. Joseph Palmer, for the best heifer, the property of a tenaat farmer : S. W. Gould; r, Norcott. Silver Cup (value £5) given by Mr. Johl Coxon, for the best shire brood mare, the property of a tenant farmer: Mr. James Gould. _ -</p>
        <p>Silver Cup (value £5) given by Mr. A. B. Boumphrey, for the best hunter gelding or filly : T. A. Owen. Spwial Prizes £5 an.l £2 given by Mr. J. Whittaker, Kenworthy, for the best shire foals sired by any of his horses : 1, T. W.rburton ;2, T. Southern. Special Prizes of £2 and £l, given by Warrington Shire Horse Society. for best two colt foals: 1, Z. Billington ; 2,J. Wbitlow. Special Prize of £2 and .Cl, given by Warrington Sarre Horse Society for best filly foals, sired by the Shire Stallion' Special Brand " : 1. J. L)ngshaw ;2, J. Whitlow.</p>
        <p>Premum of £5 given by Cheshire Hnnt Covert Fund for the best Hunter Brood Mare, the property of a tenant farmer: Joseph Millington. Special prize of £3 given by Messrs. Henry Milling and Co., Ltd., for the Lest white cheesa : T. Dawson. Prize offered by Messrs. Day and Son, Crewe, for best Dairy Cow in Calf, the property of a tenant farmer: D. Massey. Prize offered by Messrs. Barmaak, Ltd., Manchester, for best Bull under two years, the property of a tenant farmer : S.S. Rain,gill. Gold Medal (value £10) offered by the Shire Horse Society for best Mare or Filly exhibited by members of the Warrington Agricultural Society: James Gould. Silver Medal offered by the Hunters' Improvement Society for the best Hunter Filly : Thcnias Prescott. Silver Medal offered by the Hunters' Improvement Society for the best Hunter Mare or Gelding: It Needham. Silver Medal offered by the Hackney Horse Society for the best Hackney or Pony Mare, Filly or Filly Foal: W. Johnson.</p>
