      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-08-21_WidnesExaminer_art0064" n="art0064">
        <head>KING AT IWARIENBAD.</head>
        <p>THE KING AT IWARIENBAD.</p>
        <p>The King is taking the cure at Marienbad. Each morning in his room at the Rotel Weimar he drinks a glass of Kreuzbrunner water, after which be walks down to the Promenade where he takes a second glass. His Majesty, who is in improved health and Spirits, mixes freely with the crowds on the Promenade, who stare at him, it is true, but quite respectfully and from a distance. The vis.tors to Marienbad—:specially the Americans—find it matter for great wonder that the King of Englind :hould wish to be regarded as a private individual, His Majesty's visit to Marienbad, i! is hopel, will tend to relieve the tension that has existed 1-etween Austria and Great Britain during the past few months. In our photograph the King is accompanied by Co:onel Ponsonby and the Hon. Seymour Fortescue.</p>
