      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-08-21_WidnesExaminer_art0065" n="art0065">
        <head>STRIKE IN SWEDEN.</head>
        <p>STRIKE IN SWEDEN.</p>
        <p>0 ' Herr Hjalmar Branting, the well-known !-abour leader, is at the head of the strikers lu Sweden. Work is being gradually re- sumed, but the number of strikers is given at three hundred thousand.</p>
        <p>J'</p>
        <p>--,kai.</p>
        <p>RETURN OF THE TERRITORIALS.</p>
        <p>The Territorials are home aga'n. They have drilled and marched under scorching vans, and they have entered with great enthcsilEm into the work that had to be done; and it is to be supposed they are returning to the desk and bench much better soldiers than they were a month ago. It has been suggested that the period in camp should have culminated with a great display that would have enabled the public to realise something of the object to which their training tends, and it is expected that by another year something of the kind will be arranged., Our illustration shows a number of Loudon Territorigls on their way home boardiug a motor-bus in the Strand.</p>
        <p>(3) Are you looking old before your time?</p>
        <p>(4) Are you sensitive and irritable? (5) Do you feel weak after exertion? (6) Have you kidney and digestive troubles? (7) Are you losing flesh?</p>
        <p>contrasted with the cheers for Mr: Lloyd George, gave the hesitating chairman encouragement. Presently he read a resolution condemning the Budget and,commending Tariff Reform. The show of hands in its favour was not at all solid. The speakers and others on the platform looked anxious. The chair- man dallied in putting the alternative, until the crowd insisted on this being done, and the chairman had no option but to comply. He took at last the vote against the resolution, and smiled unhappily at the spectacle of more than two-thirds of the meeting voting solidly against him. Then there went up great cheers for the Budget and for Mr. Lloyd George.— " Westminster Gazette."</p>
